            <div xml:id="d494">

                <pb facs="0688" n="564" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg564"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.1211/199a</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Summerlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-11-07"><hi rendition="#italic">November 7,
                        1923</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2539</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department encloses herewith, for your
                    information and the confidential files of the Embassy, two volumes containing
                    signed <pb facs="0689" n="565" xml:id="pg565"/> copies of the minutes in English
                    and Spanish of the recent conferences in Mexico City between the Commissioners
                    representing the United States and the Mexican Commissioners.</p>
                <p>In this connection, there is also enclosed, for your information and discreet
                    use, a copy of a statement which the Department has made public with regard to
                    the General and Special Claims Conventions which are recorded in the minutes. In
                    view of the fact that these Conventions are to be submitted to the United States
                    Senate for its assent, the Department is not in a position to make any further
                    statement with respect to them at this particular time. The Department will
                    advise you from time to time of any additional important information which it
                    may give out regarding the minutes of the conferences.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William
                            Phillips</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d494-a1.xml" xpointer="d494-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
